{{!
    @template mod_booking/slotbooking/slot_update_success

    Final page of the self-service move/cancel dialog.

    The prepage's own "Booking complete" page cannot serve this flow: it only ever says "booked",
    and loading it re-books a user who is no longer in a booked state (see
    bo_info::load_pre_booking_page()), which after a cancellation would undo the cancellation.
    The wording therefore comes from the caller, which knows what actually happened.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * message - What happened, already localised, e.g. "Your slot has been moved to ...".
    * closelabel - Label of the close button.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "message": "Your slot has been moved to Tuesday, 8 September 2026 · 9:30 AM - 10:00 AM.",
        "closelabel": "Close"
    }
}}
<div class="condition-confirmation mb-1 mt-1 p-2 text-center bg-light border border-secondary rounded">
    {{message}}
</div>
<div class="d-flex justify-content-end mt-3">
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-action="slotupdate-close">{{closelabel}}</button>
</div>
